s up the module by the canonicalized package\ndocs/concepts/hooks-and-overrides.rst|47|name.  If the module defines the requested method, it is called instead\ndocs/concepts/hooks-and-overrides.rst|48|of the default; otherwise the default runs.\ndocs/concepts/hooks-and-overrides.rst|49|\ndocs/concepts/hooks-and-overrides.rst:50:Override hooks cover resolution, source acquisition, building,\ndocs/concepts/hooks-and-overrides.rst|51|dependency extraction, and build environment customization.  Third-party\ndocs/concepts/hooks-and-overrides.rst|52|packages register overrides via the ``fromager.project_overrides``\ndocs/concepts/hooks-and-overrides.rst|53|entry-point group in their ``pyproject.toml``, mapping a package name to\ndocs/concepts/hooks-and-overrides.rst|54|a Python module.\ndocs/concepts/hooks-and-overrides.rst|55|\ndocs/concepts/hooks-and-overrides.rst:56:See :doc:`/reference/hooks` for the complete list of hooks and their\ndocs/concepts/hooks-and-overrides.rst|57|arguments.\ndocs/concepts/hooks-and-overrides.rst|58|\ndocs/concepts/hooks-and-overrides.rst:59:Global Hooks\ndocs/concepts/hooks-and-overrides.rst|60|------------\ndocs/concepts/hooks-and-overrides.rst:62:Global hooks are event callbacks that fire for every package.  All\ndocs/concepts/hooks-and-overrides.rst|63|registered plugins for a hook are called sequentially.  They cannot\ndocs/concepts/hooks-and-overrides.rst|64|alter the build result — they are purely side-effecting notifications.\ndocs/concepts/hooks-and-overrides.rst|65|\ndocs/concepts/hooks-and-overrides.rst:80:Third-party packages register hooks via the ``fromager.hooks``\ndocs/concepts/hooks-and-overrides.rst|81|entry-point group in their ``pyproject.toml``, mapping a hook name to\ndocs/concepts/hooks-and-overrides.rst|82|a callable.\ndocs/concepts/hooks-and-overrides.rst|83|\ndocs/concepts/hooks-and-overrides.rst:84:See :doc:`/customization` for examples and argument details.\ndocs/concepts/hooks-and-overrides.rst|85|\ndocs/concepts/package-settings.rst:1:Package Settings\ndocs/concepts/package-settings.rst|2|================\ndocs/concepts/package-settings.rst:4:Fromager uses a layered settings system to configure how each package\ndocs/concepts/package-settings.rst|5|is resolved, downloaded, patched, and built.  Settings flow from YAML\ndocs/concepts/package-settings.rst|6|files on disk through a merge pipeline into a single facade object\ndocs/concepts/package-settings.rst|7|used by the build pipeline.\ndocs/concepts/package-settings.rst|8|\ndocs/concepts/package-settings.rst:14:Settings Loading Flow\ndocs/concepts/package-settings.rst|15|---------------------\ndocs/concepts/package-settings.rst:36:package is queried and cached for the rest of the run.\ndocs/concepts/package-settings.rst|37|\ndocs/concepts/package-settings.rst:38:Directory Structure\ndocs/concepts/package-settings.rst|39|-------------------\ndocs/concepts/package-settings.rst:50:       ├── torch/                 # Unversioned (all versions)\ndocs/concepts/package-settings.rst:57:Package YAML filenames use the canonicalized package name (lowercase,\ndocs/concepts/package-settings.rst|58|hyphens).  All three directories are configurable via CLI flags.\ndocs/concepts/package-settings.rst|59|\ndocs/concepts/package-settings.rst:60:Merge Order\ndocs/concepts/package-settings.rst|61|-----------\ndocs/concepts/package-settings.rst:63:Settings are merged from least-specific to most-specific.  Later\ndocs/concepts/package-settings.rst|64|layers override earlier ones:\ndocs/concepts/package-settings.rst|65|\ndocs/concepts/package-settings.rst:79:   │     (env vars, pre_built, wheel_server_url)      │\ndocs/concepts/package-settings.rst:88:For environment variables specifically, the merge order within a\ndocs/concepts/package-settings.rst|89|single ``get_extra_environ()`` call is: parallel-jobs settings, build\ndocs/concepts/package-settings.rst|90|environment paths, package-level ``env``, then variant-level ``env``.\ndocs/concepts/package-settings.rst|91|Entries can reference earlier values using ``$VAR`` template syntax.\ndocs/concepts/package-settings.rst|92|\ndocs/concepts/package-settings.rst:93:PackageBuildInfo Facade\ndocs/concepts/package-settings.rst|94|-----------------------\ndocs/concepts/package-settings.rst:97:query all package configuration.  It wraps a ``PackageSettings`` and\ndocs/concepts/package-settings.rst|98|adds variant awareness, patch discovery, and template resolution.\ndocs/concepts/package-settings.rst|99|\ndocs/concepts/package-settings.rst:125:See :doc:`/reference/config-reference` for the full field reference.\ndocs/concepts/package-settings.rst|126|","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01QDYsEQHrDTDqxN7B7bSQ4G","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"rule"}}]}
